/**
 * بدل الكلمة's 3-letter Arabic word bank — validates every submitted
 * word entirely client-side, no network call per move (see
 * app/bidal/solo/page.tsx's attemptMove).
 *
 * SOURCE: MustafaLinux/arabic-words-list (MIT licensed) —
 * https://github.com/MustafaLinux/arabic-words-list — 3.5M+ Arabic
 * words extracted from real published books (لسان العرب، تاج العروس،
 * ~7,000 books from المكتبة الشاملة). Filtered here to exactly-3-letter
 * entries after normalization (see normalizeBidalWord below), deduped,
 * with only the most obvious noise removed (double-hamza sequences,
 * a letter tripled 3x — neither occurs in real Arabic).
 *
 * HONEST LIMITATION: the source itself estimates ~90% accuracy (OCR
 * artifacts, occasional merged/misspelled entries from book-scanning —
 * see the repo's own README). This is real Arabic vocabulary at real
 * scale, not a hand-picked "safe" list — which also means a small
 * fraction of entries may be OCR noise rather than genuine words. If
 * players report a specific bad entry, it's a one-line removal from
 * BIDAL_WORD_STRING below, not a rebuild of the approach.
 *
 * WHY NORMALIZATION MATTERS HERE SPECIFICALLY: بدل's drawable letters
 * (lib/bidal-letters.ts's LETTER_WEIGHTS) only ever include bare ا ه ي
 * ء — never أ/إ/آ (hamza-on-alef), ة (teh marbuta), ى (alef maksura),
 * or ئ/ؤ (hamza-on-ya/waw). A player physically cannot place tiles
 * spelling "شفة" with its real teh marbuta — they can only ever spell
 * "شفه". Every word below is normalized the same way (fold to the
 * letters actually in the game's tile bag) specifically so real words
 * using those forms still validate against what a player can actually
 * type, instead of being incorrectly rejected for an orthographic
 * detail the game's own letter bag makes impossible to reproduce.
 */

